<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Middle East Live: US strikes Iran for first time in a month as Tehran retaliates against Jordan base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7798eb42f1e95b36dd3393d8f4c5b9964f182c9e83aab9b222db7cfa034d556e</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T23:02:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-middle-east-live-us-strikes-iran-for-first-time-in-a-month" /><summary type="html">US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in their first military action in a month on Sunday, breaking a lull in fighting during an intermittent war that has lasted more than six months. Iran swiftly vowed to retaliate for what it called a deadly attack. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US forces strike Iranian launchers on Larak island in Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74092eb25b59c198efbaefe4cf6da07cf18abced9cece9cab2f56476de31d96c</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T20:27:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-us-forces-strike-iranian-launchers-on-larak-island-in-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in the first military action in a month, a US official said Sunday. ⁠Iran's ⁠Revolutionary ​Guards ​said the attack on Larak ​island ‌killed and wounded ⁠several Iranian fighters and ​civilians, and ‌vowed to punish those ​responsible.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu condemns violence in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc97542ccc1d8e586a2a1ba963d1bf3fd130723c0e37a9fbbbbccaed99b2b862</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T08:46:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-condemns-violence-in-west-bank--f146c0bf0b9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-condemns-violence-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">It was a rare condemnation from what is widely seen as the most religious and ultranationalist government in Israel’s history. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu condemned recent attacks by Israeli settlers on Palestinians in the occupied West Bank, but described the violence as the actions of a “handful of rioters.” Tensions have surged across the territory, with activists accusing settlers of acting with impunity. Much of the recent violence has taken place in the town of Qusra. Peter O’Brien reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu condemns 'criminal acts of violence' by settlers in West Bank villages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:348364db68f0f9b34fc60e3125a60992e3eac99862821e0cd1deb99f5cd89cae</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T18:34:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260829-netanyahu-condemns-criminal-acts-of-violence-by-settlers-in-west-bank-villages--94a13b44b42b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260829-netanyahu-condemns-criminal-acts-of-violence-by-settlers-in-west-bank-villages" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Saturday condemned what he called "criminal acts of violence" perpetrated by Israeli settlers in two Palestinian villages. Earlier in August, a group of settlers blocked supplies from entering Palestinian houses on the outskirts of Qusra and attacked a Palestinian family and a foreign media crew in nearby Jalud.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war reaches 6-month mark: Conflict cost $1,100 per US taxpayer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a4922d40e09c8b3d26390b420be9af073f405a7eeb5c32f0d3ebb4f4538ec54</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T15:24:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-war-reaches-6-month-mark-conflict-cost-1-100-per-us-taxpayer--0914f5e1ed99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-war-reaches-6-month-mark-conflict-cost-1-100-per-us-taxpayer" /><summary type="html">After six months of war, Iran’s leadership has coalesced around a hard core of military generals and clerics long entrenched in the ruling theocracy. They are ready for a potentially long confrontation with the US and determined to prevent any unrest at home. It’s a far cry from US President Donald Trump’s initial hopes of toppling the Islamic Republic and his subsequent claims that “regime change” had brought more compromising officials to the fore. In an analysis, FRANCE 24's Philip Turle said the war had so far cost around 1,100 US dollars for each US taxpayer.</summary></entry><entry><title>Situation in Niger 'not stabilised yet' as security forces deploy around airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bea67327cf9280d51b5cd021631209eaf33acc6941f6b2f23f334f6e0c0cddd</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T13:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/situation-in-niger-not-stabilised-yet-as-security-forces-deploy-around-airport--ef7479b2be5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/situation-in-niger-not-stabilised-yet-as-security-forces-deploy-around-airport" /><summary type="html">A group of soldiers in Niger rebelled against officers at a key military base and fired at sensitive locations in the capital, Niamey, in an apparent mutiny marked by gunfire and explosions, authorities said Saturday, in what was seen as a major threat to the country's struggling junta. FRANCE 24's Wassim Nasr brings you this analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>Several killed in Israeli strikes on Gaza and West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ba1a8b8383e10e3667797aab9a595f9ba1fcf6866f06600c9b490f4bd27eab9</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T10:34:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/several-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-gaza-and-west-bank--999317521e97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/several-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-gaza-and-west-bank" /><summary type="html">Israeli strikes in Gaza have killed five people, local hospital officials said Friday. Two brothers and another relative died in a strike on the family’s home outside Khan Younis, officials at Nasser Hospital said. Two separate Israeli strikes killed one person each in Gaza City, according to health officials at Shifa hospital.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel army carries out rare West Bank air strike, killing 'three terrorists'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f88ca6257a667aad17f5f010932040772e0d3503ee12f74af78226cb01f0250e</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T17:14:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-israel-army-carries-out-rare-west-bank-air-strike-killing-three-terrorists--652d71ff42af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-israel-army-carries-out-rare-west-bank-air-strike-killing-three-terrorists" /><summary type="html">Israel's military said it carried out an air strike in the Jenin area in the West Bank on Friday that killed a ​Palestinian it described as a Hamas militant operative as well as two of his accomplices, in a rare use of deadly Israeli air power in the occupied territory.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>There is no proof that this video shows a plane crash in Tel Aviv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d8dc2573215467a78e8bee7d3bbe1158619f598a8cb68058399fc35231d248a</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T15:31:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-no-proof-video-shows-plane-crash-tel-aviv--6a155fc46fc5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-no-proof-video-shows-plane-crash-tel-aviv" /><summary type="html">A video showing an airplane rammed into the side of a building has been circulating widely on social media. While social media users are claiming that the video shows a plane that crashed in Tel Aviv after an Iranian attack, its origin remains unknown and its authenticity highly questionable.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's 'retrospective incrimination: First we shoot, we kill &amp; then find a reason why it happened'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77ef7b4bae090098efb124065b7dad921b8804a297327ede3a96c5ae20c66300</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T08:58:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/retrospective-incrimination-first-we-shoot-we-kill-and-then-we-find-a-reason-why-it-happened--b52d3a0f8d9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/retrospective-incrimination-first-we-shoot-we-kill-and-then-we-find-a-reason-why-it-happened" /><summary type="html">Liza Kaminov is pleased to welcome Nadav Weiman, Executive Director of Breaking the Silence. He says there is a troubling gap between how Israeli military operations in Gaza are publicly explained and what soldiers experience on the ground. Testimonies collected by Breaking the Silence suggest that this gap is not simply about individual incidents, but about the policies, assumptions and rules of engagement. The testimony surrounding the Nasser Hospital strike points to “retrospective incrimination”: rather than identifying a legitimate military target before an attack, evidence connecting those killed to Hamas may be sought afterward in order to justify the strike.</summary></entry><entry><title>Syria President appoints Kurdish leader Mazloum Abdi as presidential adviser</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05f84eb643e9fcedd290b281e84401d309c899d098ac48b75d00c5f222675e14</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T21:59:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-syria-president-appoints-kurdish-leader-mazloum-abdi-as-presidential-adviser--c1507ae482bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-syria-president-appoints-kurdish-leader-mazloum-abdi-as-presidential-adviser" /><summary type="html">Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa appointed Kurdish leader Mazloum Abdi as an adviser to the presidency, state media said on Friday. Abdi's appointment comes just days after he dissolved the Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces (SDF) as part of an integration agreement with Damascus.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran, Qatar hold Hormuz talks as US blockade squeezes Iran oil exports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f97cebb1b67518c146139be258fef4d3873c1bb6d53521b0e40a8506dd7d018</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:01:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-iran-qatar-hold-hormuz-talks-as-us-blockade-chokes-iran-oil-imports--6823e5b7309d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-iran-qatar-hold-hormuz-talks-as-us-blockade-chokes-iran-oil-imports" /><summary type="html">Officials from Iran and Qatar met on Thursday in Tehran for diplomatic talks on the strategic Strait of Hormuz, as a US naval blockade chokes oil supplies to Iran amid a domestic shortfall. The meetings follow a week of intense diplomacy in Iran involving separate meetings with officials from Oman and Pakistani seeking ways to end the war and reopen Hormuz.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Driven by faith, Jewish activists stand up to settlers to protect West Bank Palestinians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b20f3a846776ae5a56ebbce618fa76c6262975616d1785133c06a2a836e1616</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T09:41:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-driven-by-faith-jewish-activists-stand-up-to-settlers-to-protect-west-bank-palestinians--d5b96a52f18a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-driven-by-faith-jewish-activists-stand-up-to-settlers-to-protect-west-bank-palestinians" /><summary type="html">A group of Israelis who regularly travel to the West Bank to protect Palestinians who are victims of increasing attacks by settlers say their Jewish faith drove them towards activism. On Tuesday, at least five activists were injured while rushing to assist Palestinians being harassed by settlers in the village of Jannatah, near Bethlehem.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Navigation, jurisdiction, costs: Iran, Oman attempt to hammer out Hormuz deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d53f31c0c6cb09e59213f18c5e9e87c31d0de06bfe4653e31f21a1c643c1749b</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T20:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-navigation-jurisdiction-costs-iran-oman-attempt-to-hammer-out-hormuz-deal--a233044920da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-navigation-jurisdiction-costs-iran-oman-attempt-to-hammer-out-hormuz-deal" /><summary type="html">Iran and Oman are holding talks to try to reach an interim agreement for a controlled resumption of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz. The two countries have discussed a framework for a “temporary corridor” for shipping, according to a joint statement by the Iranian and Omani foreign ministries. But the plan faces several hurdles.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Syria: Why is the dissolution of the Kurdish forces significant?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d46471279eb14c73a3aa790172cc25cc87874f845d2b32d0e1b020dd2ec508cd</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T16:16:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260826-syria-why-is-the-dissolution-of-the-kurdish-forces-significant--a05f8cfc7a2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260826-syria-why-is-the-dissolution-of-the-kurdish-forces-significant" /><summary type="html">The Syrian Kurdish Forces announced their dissolution on August 25, in what is considered a significant step for Syria. FRANCE 24's Andrew Hilliar tells us why.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says he believes Iran’s leader is still alive but 'seriously wounded'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b785681b790edf1920246b706e84f99bf2e77920d02068df6caea92a8b15412</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T06:04:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-middle-east-live-iran-says-hormuz-strait-still-closed-despite-transit-corridor-talks-with-o--b561458c24a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-middle-east-live-iran-says-hormuz-strait-still-closed-despite-transit-corridor-talks-with-oman" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Wednesday said he believes Iran’s Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei is “very seriously wounded”, but not dead. Khamenei has not been seen in public since the US and Israel launched the Iran war in February, prompting months of speculation over the new Iranian leader’s health. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US-led Gaza peace board warns Hamas over kites after Israeli threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8bde9dbab6abbe3d723be3a2129f691644efe58edad5021c29054fa298604a2</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T21:49:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-us-gaza-peace-board-hamas-kites-israeli-threat--526ad678f67e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-us-gaza-peace-board-hamas-kites-israeli-threat" /><summary type="html">The US-led board overseeing the Gaza peace plan warned Hamas on Tuesday to halt militant activity, including flying kites, after Israel threatened retaliatory strikes. A Board of Peace official said Israel must also respect the ceasefire, limiting military action to responses to “genuine and imminent threats.”</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Syrian Kurdish leader announces SDF dissolution after its integration into army</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ada5072121d94041a4095a0272ff78025d62311d0c2581da3714e18b3c2870e</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T18:49:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-syrian-kurdish-leader-dissolves-force-that-spearheaded-jihadist-fight--3b0b10c38d52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-syrian-kurdish-leader-dissolves-force-that-spearheaded-jihadist-fight" /><summary type="html">Mazloum Abdi, the commander-in-chief of the Syrian Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces (SDF) on Tuesday announced the dissolution of the group in a televised speech from the presidential palace in Damascus. The dissolution followed the integration of SDF fighters into the Syrian military, said Abdi, and represented a major victory for Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran offers $10 million to kill Trump's son</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b93b4a07042e8ea6d17240f58b42459ce2ac2feff539028f9726225a2656607</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T15:44:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-offers-10-million-to-kill-trump-s-son--e32b74674cd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-offers-10-million-to-kill-trump-s-son" /><summary type="html">Iranian state media has aired a video that appears to threaten the life of Barron Trump, US President Donald Trump's youngest son. Since the start of the war in February, Iranian media have on multiple occasions circulated content threatening the president and family members.  The US Secret Service has confirmed it is aware of the video.</summary></entry><entry><title>US economic D-Day sanctions: 'Repeated bombing attacks across Iran failed to change the calculus'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51ec5182556b2138c76922b543f9f289ad099f9001019da3c8feccaef920ecbb</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T13:44:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260825-us-economic-d-day-sanctions-repeated-bombing-attacks-across-iran-failed-to-change-the-calcu--31fcda056165.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260825-us-economic-d-day-sanctions-repeated-bombing-attacks-across-iran-failed-to-change-the-calculus" /><summary type="html">Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Imran Bayoumi, Deputy Director &amp; Resident Fellow at the Atlantic Council. He sees the Trump administration’s new sanctions strategy toward Iran as an attempt to seek economic leverage where military force has so far failed to produce any results. But its effectiveness rests on several unresolved assumptions. Chief among them is whether Washington can compel China, Iran’s largest oil customer, to comply despite Beijing’s growing economic resilience. Iran, meanwhile, has decades of experience curtailing sanctions and is again threatening regional escalation.</summary></entry><entry><title>With sanctions and tariffs, US bets on its economic power to get what it wants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24ad8fcc83c89c53e0a6cf6fe3b9a6d992d9aeed968959262b76426e523b4dc4</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T13:25:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/with-sanctions-and-tariffs-us-bets-on-its-economic-power-to-get-what-it-wants--9bf5430da6c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/with-sanctions-and-tariffs-us-bets-on-its-economic-power-to-get-what-it-wants" /><summary type="html">The US has announced a new wave of sanctions on Iran and has promised to sanction any countries trading with it - including China. It also comes as the US deepens a trade war with its neighbour Canada. FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US removes Syria off its list of state sponsors of terrorism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6fecd2becdbde8569e65e049f08ecd21cd6eaa480f9575334340bf759bacbd9c</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T13:18:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-removes-syria-off-its-list-of-state-sponsors-of-terrorism--dbdce8d61adc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-removes-syria-off-its-list-of-state-sponsors-of-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Turkey has welcomed a US decision to remove Syria from its list of state sponsors of terrorism. The move rescinds a decades-old designation which came with severe economic consequences for Damascus. Corresponding sanctions relief for Syria have also been announced.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran threatens retaliation as new US sanctions hit already-struggling economy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a96247b3cf09e2af5a1b710cffe986cb58e3e28e4337eda4b8ca3434015ddf7</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T09:36:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-threatens-retaliation-as-new-us-sanctions-hit-already-struggling-economy--2c7473d7a02f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-threatens-retaliation-as-new-us-sanctions-hit-already-struggling-economy" /><summary type="html">Iranian officials are maintaining their strong rhetoric against the US, after Washington announced a fresh raft of sanctions against Iran. Tehran has pledged to hit back with its own measures, while the country is already suffering from already high inflation.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says Strait of Hormuz demined, warns of ‘zero tolerance’ for new mines</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1803b58a9267e05f66e5026f2c10c1e38deca4d60b4e0a7c128a392bc89ff8db</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T03:31:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-mideast-live-oil-tanker-struck-by-projectile-in-strait-of-hormuz-off-oman--870804c7ee33.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-mideast-live-oil-tanker-struck-by-projectile-in-strait-of-hormuz-off-oman" /><summary type="html">President ​Donald Trump on Tuesday said all ​mines ‌within ⁠the ‌international waters of ⁠the Strait of Hormuz ​had been ‌removed or detonated, ‌and that ​Iran had been notified that any ship ​or ​boat ​placing new ​mines would be destroyed under a US “zero tolerance policy”. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Netanyahu says Iran tried to assassinate one of his sons</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a823d5cb69d866f531d8417d9684ed1329e5ce324498dfcaa3dd6d79b92e13e</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T21:38:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260824-israel-netanyahu-says-iran-tried-kill-son--ed5b499ca128.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260824-israel-netanyahu-says-iran-tried-kill-son" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said on Monday that Iran had attempted to assassinate one of his two sons, without providing evidence or further details. “Iran tried to kill one of my sons,” Netanyahu told Israel’s Channel 14, as he discussed security arrangements ahead of the October 27 election.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Mohammed bin Salman in the City of Light: Does West value economic interests over 'Western values'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60ada048dc1be06686f1dc3befae26c69f46965ee5e8002f2addde2824dd74ca</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T16:26:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/mbs-in-the-city-of-light-in-a-world-of-realpolitik-does-west-value-economic-interests-over-values--c559c04fa853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mbs-in-the-city-of-light-in-a-world-of-realpolitik-does-west-value-economic-interests-over-values" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Susanne Koelbl, Der Spiegel's award-winning foreign correspondent. According to Koelbl,, Emmanuel Macron’s decision to welcome Mohammed bin Salman at the Élysée reflects realpolitik in its purest form: 'Saudi Arabia had become too important for energy, regional security, investment and diplomacy in the Middle East to be permanently isolated. So Macron wanted to establish France as an independent, balanced power between the Mediterranean and the Gulf."</summary></entry><entry><title>With 'rare' Paris talks, France hopes to cash in on Saudi investment programme</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:208c042215cc7e2ff5b78b8e1bf7f276e2fb84ce259caf0585ae35be9d514884</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T13:52:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/with-rare-paris-talks-france-hopes-to-cash-in-on-saudi-investment-programme--df1c195dea15.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/with-rare-paris-talks-france-hopes-to-cash-in-on-saudi-investment-programme" /><summary type="html">Saudi's crown prince Mohammed bin Salman is in Paris to meet France's President Emmanuel Macron. The two leaders are to hold talks on a variety of topics, but first and foremost about the situation in the Middle East. For France, this is a chance to benefit from Saudi Arabia's Vision 2030 investment plan. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali is at the Elysée Palace and tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>What could new US sanctions on Iran entail?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4bf7c30c3a2cdb3c4295355908a06c1ca4c18811425ca17262a5eac15314dfde</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T13:42:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-could-new-us-sanctions-on-iran-entail--71c398056903.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-could-new-us-sanctions-on-iran-entail" /><summary type="html">The US says it is preparing to announce new sanctions on Iran. It's been billed an economic D-day and is expected to add further pressure on the country's economy that's already been battered from previous sanctions and a US naval blockade. The renewed economic pressure would not be the first time the US has used economic tools at its disposal to corner Iran. But what could the new measures likely entail?</summary></entry><entry><title>US unveils expanded sanctions aimed at Iran's 'economic asphyxiation'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3dea7d0a00ca93028155c52b9063b8bc1c201ac8265b909d2f7afedc2ab25f04</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T13:27:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260824-us-unveils-fresh-sanctions-to-sever-every-economic-lifeline-sustaining-iran--e8cf01b44919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260824-us-unveils-fresh-sanctions-to-sever-every-economic-lifeline-sustaining-iran" /><summary type="html">The US on Monday announced an expansion of secondary sanctions it hopes will "sever every economic lifeline" ​that sustains ‌Iran, Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said at a press conference. The expanded sanctions target Iran's digital assets, technology, gold, aviation and shipping sectors.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran predicts ‘another defeat’ for US after Washington's new sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c83a4d7675c132208f623b1d2dac98abdce466cdab84d85161bd078a1cd88b5f</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:10Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T12:50:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260824-middle-east-live-iran-warns-of-a-harsh-response-to-anticipated-us-sanctions--0b1704bae339.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260824-middle-east-live-iran-warns-of-a-harsh-response-to-anticipated-us-sanctions" /><summary type="html">Iranian Economy Minister Ali Madanizadeh on Monday warned of "another defeat" for the US after Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent announced expanded sanctions against Tehran. Madanizadeh said Iran had a "two-year plan" to counter the new sanctions and dismissed Bessent's stated efforts to sever "every economic lifeline" sustaining Iran. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
